nodecode-fashion-design is a rewrite of priticolours's priticolours/fashion-design:
https://github.com/priticolours/fashion-design
commit 1fef81776333f8941a800e83a0db9236e0f1d82b
MIT, Copyright (c) 2026 priticolours (declared in plugin.yaml; the repository ships no LICENSE file)

The original is a Hermes Agent plugin in Python: ten tool handlers, each a pure
function over module-level tables that answers a JSON document, plus a bundled
skill file with the studio knowledge (construction basics, standard
measurements, fabric properties, grading rules, tech pack standards). This
rewrite keeps the same ten tools under the same names, the same arguments, the
same tables and the same JSON shapes, so a model that knew one knows the other;
the skill's knowledge is the manual on `(help :fashion-design)`. The seams are
Nodecode's: each tool's arguments are declared once with a contract, so the
schema the provider reads and the record the verb takes cannot disagree, and a
call that leaves out a required member is refused at the boundary. Four numbers
the original hard-coded (inches, US dollars, 12 % waste, a 2.5x retail markup)
are the cell's settings instead. Added: a `/fashion-design` command that runs
one verb from its line, and a collection plan and size sheet that answer in the
unit the section asks for.

Left out, because the harness differs: the plugin's own exception wrapper
around each handler, which answered `{"error": ...}` where this cell refuses an
unsatisfied call at its declared boundary; the unused `data/standard_measurements.json`
(the plugin's handlers read tables inline, and this cell keeps one copy of
them); and the per-tool `toolset` name, which Nodecode files under the cell's own
name.
